<title>UK: LIFFE wheat down on rain, EU export tax.</title>
<headline>LIFFE wheat down on rain, EU export tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE wheat ended lower as rain accross southern England hit new crop prices, while old crop months were forced down by the EU's decision to tax wheat exports, traders said.</p>
<p>January was most active with 158 of a total 449 lots. It last traded 1.60 stg lower at 98.00 stg.</p>
<p>There were no barley futures traded at all.</p>
<p>Physical grains markets were quiet, traders said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
